@page "/bathroom"
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components

<h1>Public Restrooms</h1>
<p>How to find and use public toilets in Thailand (mock info for the MVP).</p>

<div class="card">
    <h3>Where to find them</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>Malls (Central, MBK, ICONSIAM) — clean, free, often with attendants.</li>
        <li>Convenience stores (7-Eleven, FamilyMart) — ask the counter for the key.</li>
        <li>BTS / MRT stations — paid (around 2–4 THB) or free at some exits.</li>
        <li>Temples and markets — varying cleanliness; carry tissue just in case.</li>
    </ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
    <h3>Tips</h3>
    <p>Always carry a small pack of tissues or hand sanitizer — paper and soap are not guaranteed. Public restrooms are usually squat or Western style; both are common.</p>
</div>
